mitch  morris and all that but the defense i do  think the moves they're making will help  their football team  well and you know i was talking to  somebody last week at the league  meetings about the chiefs and why their  defense was not as good as it needed to  be and you know the offense and the  defense do  work together and  if you're scoring too quickly right  late in the game  you're putting more pressure on your  defense to try to stop the other team  from scoring and we criticize the chiefs  from time to time when it comes to their  ability to manage the clock because they  take too long sometimes you could argue  they score too quickly and that results  in added stress for the defense but it  all you know when you talk about  situational football it's not just what  you do  when you have the ball it's thinking  about what's going to happen when you  don't have the ball that broader sense  of how much time is left what are the  circumstances and how do we thread this  all together so we have more points than  the other team when the game ends yeah  no exactly right it's a team sport and  you do have to marry kind of how you  play your offense and defense together  to  kind of have a cohesive football team  that makes sense now the thing with the  kansas city chiefs is i mean their  defense it wasn't good at anything yet  last year other than sax yes because a  lot of the times patrick mahomes and  andy reid in that offense would get out  to a lead to where yeah d4 justin  houston all they had to worry about was  rushing the passer there was nothing  else to worry about but when the games  were equal or even they couldn't really  stop anything they couldn't cover  anybody in the back end they messed up  things schematically as far as rules and  things like that and then they couldn't  stop the run to go along with it so i  think the one thing we're seeing is  where they might not be as good as  rushing off the edge i think they're  maybe putting a little more uh  eggs in the basket of let's be bigger up  front and more physical and maybe take  away the run game and we'll push the  pocket instead of trying to get d ford  and justin houston around the edge to to  annoy quarterbacks  yeah i mean the bottom line is those 52  sacks what did it all yeah it didn't do  crap exactly right right i mean it's  it's a stack that looks pretty  you got your d4 offsides on the play  that uh  on the play that ultimately could have  clinched the super bowl berth but you  know that that stuff happens and and  ford has owned that but the bottom line  is  we assume that you need to have  a great pass rush if you want to be a  great defense and a great team in  today's nfl and there's such a premium  placed on pass rushers maybe there's an  argument to be made that if you have an  overall great defense  you don't need to be racking up big sack  numbers that you know if you have good  coverage on the back end uh you don't  have to be knocking the quarterback down  to get off the field you can just play  you can play good defense and and result  in more incomplete passes and more  drives ended that way so i think it all  does kind of tie together offense and  defense front end of your defense back  into your defense chris and the chiefs  just need to do a better job of managing  the assets they have so that when the  game is over they do have more points in  the other team that's the bottom line  their offense is good enough to get them  there now their defense has to step up  but their offense also has to be  conscious of the fact that the defense  may need some help by way of game  management helping the offense can maybe  better provide yeah there was some game  certainly this year where the offense  you'd go gosh i wish andy reed and  company would  run the ball a little bit more right man  they're dominating dominating the  offensive line of scrimmage you know run  the ball chew up some time ru you know  rest your defense a little bit but again  it's hard i know that as a pike caller  being andy reid because he goes okay  yeah we got five yards but damn when we  drop back to pass we could go for 60 or  70 yards and that's that's enticing and  awesome and all that but yes i think the  patience of the run game will help out  the overall prospects of the team and to  what you're saying mike too about the  pass rush you know hey pass rushers are  real good i i understand that and you  want to be able to create pressure but  at the same time the buffalo bills the  number two defense in football you know  they were what uh 36 sacks they were  below the middle of the league the  dallas cowboys we talk about their great  front four yeah well they were like in  the middle of the league in sacks too  what they did have was a front four that  could get there and be annoying and then  they always had seven guys in past  passing lanes to make things even extra  annoying for the quarterback to make  decisions  all right we're going to take a break  when we return yesterday we did a draft  of the teams that we think will exceed  the vegas projected win totals for 2019.  today we're going to draft the teams  that we think will come under their  projected win totals we'll do that next  right here on pft live  [Music]  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

